---
description: Non-negotiable Salon product and domain invariants
alwaysApply: true
---

- Treat `docs/MARKETPLACE_REQUIREMENTS.md` as product direction and `docs/PRODUCT_SPEC.md` as the implementation source of truth; do not silently broaden scope.
- Account status is `active` or `suspended`. Self-serve signup creates an active account with exactly one marketplace role (entertainer XOR venue). Staff may suspend/reactivate; there is no staff account-approval wait to enter the marketplace.
- Model venues as organizations with owner/member membership. One account holds one role type only (no dual-role).
- Enforce role-segregated discovery on the server: entertainers discover venues/opportunities only; venues discover entertainers only; staff may moderate both.
- Unverified profiles (publication not staff-approved) are invisible in discovery. Active members may search the opposite side before verification, but may not contact (apply / send or respond to direct requests) until their own profile is verified.
- Keep contact values hidden until shortlist or accepted direct request.
- Route applications and direct requests into one booking state machine.
- Confirm only after both parties sign the current agreement version; deposit status is independent.
- German agreement text controls; English is a labeled convenience translation.
- Confirmed bookings block both calendars. Holds expire. Never permit overlapping confirmed resource bookings.
- Do not add public directories/events/reviews, chat, payments/escrow, live legal claims, or automatic verification without a spec change.
- External calendar sync is a separate milestone; do not claim it operational until provisioned.
